{
    "background_story": "Mira was a free-spirited artist, known for her whimsical and often provocative installations. Her latest project, 'Sticky Situations,' featured a massive roll of flypaper as the centerpiece. The idea was to represent the way people get stuck in their own problems, much like flies on sticky paper. As Mira worked tirelessly to bring her vision to life, she found herself becoming increasingly entangled in her own creative process. The flypaper, once a symbol of her art, began to feel like a metaphor for her own life. She felt stuck, unable to move forward or escape the pressures of her own expectations. Just as she was about to give up, Mira had an epiphany - she would use the flypaper to create a new piece, one that represented breaking free from the very things that held her back. And so, 'Sticky Situations' evolved into 'Flight,' a powerful exploration of liberation and creative freedom.",
